1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,000
A methane alert is a starting point.
What does the evidence establish?

2
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:18,000
MethaneResponse makes a scoped review inspectable.
Historical data · not a live feed

3
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Start with a traceable historical source.
Search the historical source directory.
KAZ_S_159 · UNEP MARS snapshot

4
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:40,000
Source metadata is context.
It does not establish physical mitigation.

5
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:54,000
Three discrete EnMAP observations.
Reported flux and uncertainty stay attached.

6
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:04,000
The action is catalogued in July 2026.
Its exact date is not in this casebook.

7
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:18,000
Feedback is administrative metadata.
It does not prove repair.

8
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:31,000
Choose the event and period first.
Unapplied scope is not assessed.

9
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:46,000
Apply an explicit scope.
Dates here are inclusive UTC calendar days.

10
00:01:51,000 --> 00:02:01,000
Run the deterministic rules baseline.
This is not an AI assessment.

11
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:15,000
Required reference metadata is present
for this scoped source-detection claim.

12
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:27,000
Now ask a different question:
is mitigation established in this scope?

13
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:43,000
Insufficient evidence in the submitted scope.
This does not contradict UNEP's catalogue.

14
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:56,000
The July 11 observation is not labelled
before or after the action.

15
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:09,000
Record the next evidence request:
action timestamp and linked follow-up evidence.

16
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:22,000
Export the report.
Verify the same file in the browser.

17
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:36,000
The bundle digest and context checksum match.
No blockchain receipt is included.

18
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:49,000
Change a hashed field; keep the stored digest.
The verifier reports a SHA-256 mismatch.

19
00:03:52,000 --> 00:04:00,000
Integrity helps review a record.
It does not prove physical mitigation.
